  "notes": "One garden plot of the menu, one picture per step (in this order, the plot's value picks it: 0 empty, 1 seed, 2 sprout, 3 young plant, 4 budding plant, 5 full grown (golden flower), 6 HP UP ripe, 7 POWER UP ripe). The soil itself is not in these pictures: it is the garden bed painted into the menu's ground (ts_menu_field), one 22 px cell with a low mound for each plot, so the 4 plots look like one connected bed and its edges blend into the lawn. So the first picture is empty (an empty plot shows just its mound of earth); the others draw only the seed, the plant growing up out of the mound into the top half, taller at each step, or, at the last two steps, a small dug hole with the item rising out of it (the heart = HP UP, the fist = POWER UP). The hole's earth colors are the bed's own (pal_garden's soil browns = pal_menu_field's), so it sits in the bed with no seam.",
